From a222b7330775ad5298f771d1f2e13a1bf4b923bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 07:48:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(hrd): port hrd-mockup.html to native Flutter as
 placeholder module

Ports the HTML/JS HRD (employee/payroll) mockup and its migration
instructions into the app's existing architecture, reusing every shared
component from docs/component-standards-prompt.md.

Domain (lib/features/hrd/domain/):
- payroll_engine.dart: direct port of the mockup's validated payroll
  logic (store hours, morning/evening overtime, bolong subtraction,
  Bonus Full Time, stuck-bolong detection, monthly + Friday-anchored
  weekly pay periods via one shared PayPeriod type).
- hrd_models.dart, hrd_date_utils.dart: pure-Dart models and date/label
  helpers (no Flutter/intl imports, so the engine is unit-testable as
  plain Dart).
- hrd_seed_data.dart: code-generated from the mockup's own JS data
  objects (roles, employees, attendance, payroll items, approvals,
  opening balances) rather than hand-transcribed.

Application (lib/features/hrd/application/):
- hrd_provider.dart: HrdState + HrdController owning every business
  rule (employee CRUD, role management, attendance correction with the
  stuck-bolong guard, approval sync with no ghost requests, payroll
  items, staff submissions). Includes hrdViewerModeProvider, a
  documented placeholder seam for deriving Owner vs Staff from login
  since no real auth/role system exists yet (see its doc comment).
- hrd_staff_session_provider.dart: staff PIN verification with 5-attempt
  lockout (AGENTS.md), never reveals the expected PIN.

Presentation (lib/features/hrd/presentation/):
- 11 Owner screens (Overview, Kelola Karyawan, Detail, Tambah/Edit,
  Kehadiran Hari Ini, Koreksi Absen, Riwayat Kehadiran, Tambah
  Penghasilan/Potongan, Approval, Rekap Penggajian, Rekap Kinerja, Slip
  Gaji) and 6+1 Staff screens (Pilih Nama, PIN, Dashboard, Detail
  Gaji, Riwayat, Tambah Pengeluaran, Tambah Pemasukan, Status
  Pengajuan) - UI/UX kept 1:1 with the mockup except where it
  conflicted with the component standards doc.

Fixed a latent bug found by running the mockup's own JS engine against
golden test scenarios: the original bolong-as-pulang resolution left
the stuck bolong row in place next to a new pulang row, so the day
never stopped being stuck and the approval request silently reopened.
clarifyAsPulang() here converts the bolong row into the pulang row
instead, verified in test/hrd_controller_test.dart.

Wiring:
- menu_grid_items.dart: Staff tile now opens HrdEntryScreen instead
  of the placeholder screen.
- menu_bottom_sheet.dart: Approval card now opens the real approval
  screen with a live pending count from hrdControllerProvider (was a
  dead-end pop()); added a separate Cek Gaji Saya action for the
  Staff PIN flow per the migration doc's two-entry-point requirement
  (Owner tile vs shared-device staff access). dashboard_screen.dart's
  call site updated for the resulting signature change.
- app_pin_keypad.dart: added an optional bottomLeft slot (default null,
  existing PIN screens unaffected) for the staff PIN screen's
  logout key.

Tests:
- test/hrd_payroll_engine_test.dart: golden-value tests (day scenarios,
  monthly payroll for all 6 seeded employees, Friday-anchored week
  ranges, Overview totals) - expected values produced by running the
  mockup's own JS in Node, not hand-computed.
- test/hrd_controller_test.dart: attendance-clarification and staff
  approval flow tests, including the bug fix above.

Scope note: this is an in-memory PLACEHOLDER module per AGENTS.md's
forbidden-scope entry for full HRD/payroll - nothing here is
persisted, synced, or permission-checked. Every file with structural
implications documents this explicitly (see hrd_models.dart,
hrd_provider.dart's hrdViewerModeProvider, hrd_entry_screen.dart).
